{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam configuration and documentation","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG.md",".bridge_state/projects.json","status axis","type axis","link axis","priority axis","create_defaults axis","probe command"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","migration safety","provider-neutral","mapping seam","configuration","backward compatibility"],"propositions":["The mapping seam adds new config surface and echo-safe behaviors that require authoritative documentation to guide operators and future integrators.","No capability's only trigger must be a specific CI provider; the mapping seam must work across diverse or absent CI environments to satisfy plan-review portability criterion.","The feature is additive and backward-compatible: absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior; rollback requires only section deletion.","Every mapping behavior is exercised by injected-transport unit tests with no live Jira or specific CI provider requirement; portability is substantiated by existing test suites in S1–S8.","Documentation must cover provider-neutral core as reuse seam for future targets (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) while stating direct support for those platforms is out of scope."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787873935969762001,"uuid":"7b8574d0-6146-4af4-8a48-4a82f16d418d"}